{
  "id": "grammar.a1.06.01.present-introduction",
  "title": "The regular present tense",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Talking about your day",
      "content": "The present tense lets you say what you do. Regular verbs follow a pattern. In this lesson, start with simple first-person forms such as trabajo, estudio and camino."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Simple first-person forms",
      "rows": [
        [
          "trabajar",
          "trabajo"
        ],
        [
          "estudiar",
          "estudio"
        ],
        [
          "caminar",
          "camino"
        ],
        [
          "cocinar",
          "cocino"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Trabajo por la mañana.",
          "english": "I work in the morning."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Estudio español.",
          "english": "I study Spanish."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Camino por la tarde.",
          "english": "I walk in the afternoon."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Cocino en casa.",
          "english": "I cook at home."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "The ending changes with the person. In the next lessons, you will learn the regular -ar, -er and -ir patterns."
    }
  ]
}
